Cornwall GP example: data/cornwall_*.rda, inst/extdata/cornwall_*
------------------------------------------------------------------
Built by data-raw/cornwall_gp.R from the sources below, subset to NHS
Cornwall and Isles of Scilly Integrated Care Board (QT6) and its 337 LSOA
2021 areas, joined on practice and LSOA codes and reprojected as needed.

GP registrations and workforce (cornwall_gp, cornwall_lsoa, cornwall_flows):
Patients Registered at a GP Practice (July 2026) and General Practice
Workforce (30 June 2026). Copyright (c) 2026 NHS England. Contains public
sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0,
https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/.

Small-area boundaries, population-weighted centroids and population
(cornwall_lsoa): Source: Office for National Statistics licensed under the
Open Government Licence v3.0 (LSOA 2021 boundaries with rural-urban
classification, LSOA 2021 population-weighted centroids, mid-2024 small area
population estimates via Nomis). Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and
database right 2025.

Practice locations (cornwall_gp): ONS Postcode Directory, November 2025.
Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and database right 2025. Contains Royal
Mail data (c) Royal Mail copyright and database right 2025. Source: Office
for National Statistics licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0.

Population grid (cornwall_pop.tif): WorldPop (www.worldpop.org) and the
Center for International Earth Science Information Network (CIESIN),
Columbia University (2018). Global High Resolution Population Denominators
Project, 2020 UN-adjusted 1 km estimates for the United Kingdom,
https://doi.org/10.5258/SOTON/WP00671. Licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Modifications: cropped to the
area and weighted by the share of each cell inside it.

Travel times (cornwall_travel, cornwall_gp_travel.tif): derived by the
package author from the Malaria Atlas Project 2019 global motorised friction
surface (Weiss D.J. et al. (2020) Global maps of travel time to healthcare
facilities. Nature Medicine 26, 1835-1838,
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41591-020-1059-1) with least-cost paths over land,
from the practice and centroid locations above. The Malaria Atlas Project
publishes its maps under Creative Commons Attribution: its website states
version 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/) and the Google
Earth Engine catalogue entry for the surface states version 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Both versions permit sharing
adapted material, such as these derived travel times, with attribution.
